iously gonna inform a lot of the  reviews  um but yeah also to re to read as many  perspectives as you can and  while it would be very nice for websites  to have an elder ring review from a  hardcore fan and an elden ring review  from a newbie and an elden ring review  from a middling fan um then i don't  doubt some of them will do that with  like their features or whatever  it's ultimately not cost effective  because like i said all of those people  all have jobs that aren't the review  that they have to be taken off for the  review so sometimes that means other  people have to take on my workload to  get everything done  um it's not feasible to have multiple  people reviewing games all the time i  think you would lose money um  and then people get laid off and then  there are no reviews so that doesn't  really help so  yeah i don't know i just kind of wanted  to talk about this because i thought it  was it was interesting um  probably not even going to edit this  video this is just me talking about  reviews  and biases and how they work and why i  think um fromsoft is in a really unique  spot regarding  review scores and there are other  franchises that i feel similarly about  call of duty is another one it's it is  um  probably always going to get very  similar  scores  because the audience or the people who  are interested in reviewing it  have very similar experiences and  backgrounds with first person shooters  or with call of duty itself it's just um  humans gonna human is effectively my  point  uh and i don't know i never think that  you should take reviews too seriously at  the end of the day  it is just somebody's opinion that is  that is it it is someone else's opinion  you can take it or leave it  that is up to you um  hope you enjoyed this video let me know  uh if you can think of any other games  you feel like i like inherently set up  to get like  pre-scripted review scores i think it's  an interesting one so yeah  i will see you guys next time bye
 

